("Renal 10","During bladder FILLING, which receptor pairing is active?",["M3 on the detrusor; α₁ on the sphincter","β₃ on the detrusor; α₁ on the sphincter","α₁ on the detrusor; β₃ on the sphincter","M3 on the detrusor; β₃ on the sphincter"],[1],"Storage = sympathetic: balloon relaxes (β₃), knot tied (α₁)"),
("Renal 10","A dog with a T13 spinal cord lesion has a small, spastic bladder that empties uncontrollably. Best drug?",["Bethanechol","Phenylpropanolamine","Oxybutynin","Furosemide"],[2],"Upper motor neuron = Uncontrolled squeezing → block M3 (Oxybutynin = Off)"),
("Renal 10","A spayed female dog leaks urine while sleeping; neurologic exam is normal. Best drug?",["Phenylpropanolamine","Oxybutynin","Bethanechol","Desmopressin"],[0],"Weak sphincter → α₁ agonist tightens it"),
("Renal 10","Why is phase 2 of the cystometrogram nearly flat?",["The external sphincter is relaxing","The detrusor actively relaxes as volume rises","M3 activation holds pressure constant","Urine is leaving through the internal sphincter"],[1],"Isobaric phase = storage (sympathetic β₃)"),
