("Cases","A dehydrated dog has USG 1.010 on three samples, with high BUN and creatinine. Best explanation?",["Normal kidney response to dehydration","Lost nephrons washed out the medullary gradient","Excess ADH is diluting the urine","Prerenal azotemia from low blood flow"],[1],"Persistent isosthenuria in a dry animal = can't concentrate = lost nephrons"),
("Cases","A blocked male cat has K⁺ 7.4 and pH 7.08. What comes FIRST?",["Sedate and pass a urinary catheter","Start furosemide to restore urine flow","Give bicarbonate and glucose with insulin","Start an ACE inhibitor for the kidney"],[2],"Stabilize K⁺ and acidosis before unblocking (Basel)"),
("Cases","Why does GFR fall in gentamicin acute kidney injury even though the glomerulus isn't damaged?",["Gentamicin constricts the afferent arteriole","Casts clog tubules, raising Bowman's space pressure","Gentamicin raises plasma albumin","Gentamicin lowers angiotensin II"],[1],"Starling: back pressure from clogged tubules opposes filtration"),
