("Cases","Which belongs in Basel's CKD diet for a hypertensive, wasting cat?"+SA,["Low sodium","Low phosphate","High-quality protein","Extra calcium","Extra potassium"],[0,1,2],"No extra calcium (deposits) or potassium (already trending high)"),
("Cases","A Border Collie swam all afternoon; now Na⁺, K⁺ and Cl⁻ are all low and it is seizing. Best immediate treatment?",["Spironolactone to remove water","Hypertonic saline with frequent rechecks","Desmopressin to concentrate urine","0.9% NaCl at a maintenance rate"],[1],"Diuretics are too slow; pull water out of swollen neurons now"),
("Cases","A dog drank antifreeze 1 hour ago and looks normal. What is the most specific early treatment?",["Bicarbonate fluids to correct acidosis","Ethanol to compete for the liver enzyme","Glucose and insulin for potassium","Furosemide to flush the kidneys"],[1],"Ethanol blocks conversion of ethylene glycol to its toxic metabolites"),
("Cases","A urinalysis shows protein ONLY: no glucose, no casts, normal USG. Most likely?",["Fanconi syndrome","Diabetes mellitus","Glomerular disease or urinary tract inflammation","Acute tubular necrosis"],[2],"Leaky filter delivers more protein than the proximal tubule can take back"),
("Cases","Urine shows very HIGH sodium with a low USG. Which are possible causes?"+SA,["A loop or thiazide diuretic","Hypoaldosteronism","High-volume 0.9% NaCl fluids","Hyperaldosteronism","Very low dietary salt"],[0,1,2],"Natriuresis · hyperaldosteronism and a low-salt diet would make urine sodium LOW"),
